Path parameters identify a particular resource. Query parameters usually filter, sort or paginate results.
GET /employees/101
Here, 101 is a path parameter.
GET /employees?department=IT&sort=salary
Here, department and sort are query parameters.
app.get("/employees/:id", (req, res) => {
    res.json({ employeeId: req.params.id });
});

app.get("/employees", (req, res) => {
    res.json({
        department: req.query.department,
        sort: req.query.sort
    });
});
